{
  "name": "Poison Darts",
  "type": "feature",
  "system": {
    "attribution": {},
    "description": "<p>Once per scene when a PC moves and rolls with Fear, trigger a hail of poison darts from hidden launchers. The PC and all targets within Very Close range must make an Agility Reaction Roll. On a failure, a target takes <strong>3d8+3</strong> physical damage and is <em>Dizzied</em>. <em>Dizzied</em> targets have disadvantage on their next action roll, then clear the condition.</p><section id=\"secret-E1hfNVWA3OfpXQhz\" class=\"secret\"><p><em>How did the PC accidentally trigger the trap? What mechanisms can be tinkered with to disable these traps?</em></p></section>",
